+## Literal composition (shared7)
+
+Workspace now includes a separate Literal composition panel beside the existing
+macro and semantic modes. Enter only zeroes and ones: each seven-bit word selects
+one of 79 frozen strings. IDs 79–124 are rejected; 125 undoes a literal, 126 resets
+retained source and 127 finishes. Controls have their own visible bit cost.
+Dictionary reference and known-program guides insert no source. Export/replay
+records preserve dictionary identity, events, bits, source hash and test receipts;
+imports are read-only and historical receipts are not independently authenticated.
+
+Finished source is validated only through the paired Gamma `literal_check`
+operation in its existing bounded Linux sandbox. Nothing is evaluated in the
+page. This is human binary composition, not autonomous synthesis. The frozen
+dictionary hash is
+`62ab89348d4781187375f35663f81b6304a70b9f951d9bd3327fecae6d3b8c39`.
+Gamma's `projects/algorithm_solver/literals/demo/` holds the canonical assets,
+protocol documentation, portable tests and 20-program / 3,834-case evidence.
+The original source-only benchmark excludes the new interactive controls.
+
+This sandbox panel uses `gamma.literal-shared7-interactive.v1` with control IDs
+125–127. The existing BITS typing profile remains separate with its original
+controls. Recordings from those protocols are not interchangeable.
